>>
endobj
240 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (Riverbanc was founded on a simple belief: every salaried employee deserves transparent access to financial products and the information needed to make informed financial decisions.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
241 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (Across Zambia, thousands of hardworking salaried employees contribute to the growth of our economy every day. Yet many continue to face unnecessary challenges when seeking financial solutions. Accessing loan products often involves comparing limited information, visiting multiple financial institutions, and making important financial decisions under pressure.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
242 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (Riverbanc was established in 2026 to help address these challenges through technology.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
243 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (Our objective is not to replace financial institutions, but to strengthen the relationship between participating commercial banks, licensed microfinance institutions, and the salaried employees they serve. Through our membership-based digital marketplace, Riverbanc Members are empowered to compare financial products, submit digital loan applications, explore loan refinance opportunities, and make informed borrowing decisions within a secure and transparent environment.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (As we grow, our commitment remains unchanged. We will continue to invest in technology, governance, information security, regulatory compliance, and meaningful partnerships that create sustainable value for our members and financial institution partners.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (While our journey begins in Zambia, our vision extends across Sub-Saharan Africa. We aspire to build one of Africa's most trusted financial technology marketplaces by connecting millions of salaried employees with regulated financial institutions through innovation, transparency, and responsible business practices.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
